 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Test 3, Question 1 · Marginal distributions and independence** (10 marks)",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "9a6f3cd7-0149-55f5-9844-9717e0201bb2"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "You get two random variables, $X$ and $Y$, described together: a table (discrete) or a formula $f_{X,Y}(x,y)$ (continuous). You pull out $X$ alone and $Y$ alone (the **marginals**). Then you decide if they are **independent**.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "4c3191db-e58a-58ae-ab7f-d513f72bbd57"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "tone": "tip",
   "text": "**Formula sheet lines for this question.** They are on the sheet, so a question that needs them is very likely:\n\n$$\nf_X(x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,dy\\qquad f_Y(y)=\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,dx\n$$\n\n$$\nF_X(x)=\\sum_{t\\le x}p_X(t)\\qquad F_X(x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^{x}f_X(t)\\,dt\n$$\n\nExpect: **find $c$ → a probability → marginals → independent? → a CDF**.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "3fc1fb18-7e36-5ad9-be47-5ae5fea5aca4"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Part A · Discrete (PMF tables)",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "28f8b42f-0107-560c-afa8-df8dd71f5928"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "A1 · Joint probability tables",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "c2610690-d11d-5ea6-8206-0ae3ed306f7a"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Each cell is the chance that **both** happen: $p_{X,Y}(x,y)=P(X=x,\\ Y=y)$.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "951581da-5f56-4a86-9c61-b84ad87d4f7f",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "b59dbdf2-e35b-4def-a4a6-66306282e783"
    }
   ],
   "id": "1924e247-2432-5e64-aeaf-519e6ff2f156"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "Every cell is $\\ge0$, and all cells add to $1$. An unknown $c$ comes from that.",
    "For any event, add the cells that fit it."
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "30a092de-1d2b-5adb-a56f-24bf05c9f480"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 1 · Find $c$, then add cells ★ (Lecture 17 table)",
   "prompt": "Find $c$, $P(X=1,\\ Y\\le1)$ and $P(X+Y\\le2)$.\n\n| | $y=0$ | $y=1$ | $y=2$ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $x=0$ | $0.10$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n| $x=1$ | $0.20$ | $c$ | $0.20$ |",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Find $c$:** all cells add to $1$.",
     "latex": "0.70+c=1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad c=0.30"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**$P(X=1,\\ Y\\le1)$:** row $x=1$, columns $y=0,1$.",
     "latex": "0.20+0.30=0.50"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**$P(X+Y\\le2)$:** only $(1,2)$ has $x+y>2$. Take it away from $1$.",
     "latex": "1-0.20=0.80"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$c=0.30$; $0.50$; $0.80$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "951581da-5f56-4a86-9c61-b84ad87d4f7f",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "4e7cccdb-c271-4557-95bc-41590badcef5"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "79f52518-90e0-41df-b0b0-5800904bbe9b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "a25bde00-9c60-4121-8f33-54a29f5be927"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c36d386d-ba89-50ce-a5df-f1b82d4625c5"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 1 · Build the table from an experiment",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "Toss a fair coin twice. $X$ = number of heads, $Y=1$ if the first toss is heads and $Y=0$ if not. Write the joint PMF table and find $P(X\\ge Y)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**List the 4 outcomes** (each $\\tfrac14$) as $(x,y)$: $HH\\to(2,1)$, $HT\\to(1,1)$, $TH\\to(1,0)$, $TT\\to(0,0)$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Table** (rows $x=0,1,2$, columns $y=0,1$).",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}x=0:\\ \\ \\frac14,\\ 0 \\\\ x=1:\\ \\ \\frac14,\\ \\frac14 \\\\ x=2:\\ \\ 0,\\ \\frac14\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**$P(X\\ge Y)$:** every outcome has $x\\ge y$.",
     "latex": "P(X\\ge Y)=1"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "Table above; $P(X\\ge Y)=1$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "0b2be77c-eed0-577e-9e59-8170eac92597"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "A2 · Finding marginals",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "9ad36c35-b3a8-5150-87be-c53872396e12"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "$p_X(x)$ = the chance of $X=x$ whatever $Y$ is. So add the whole row of $x$. For $p_Y$, add the column.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "951581da-5f56-4a86-9c61-b84ad87d4f7f",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "9288de14-f4e8-4c3c-8f12-d6e7473e62a7"
    }
   ],
   "id": "f795fb58-eba5-58b1-b7ae-3693442a0ac8"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "p_X(x)=\\sum_y p_{X,Y}(x,y)\\qquad\\qquad p_Y(y)=\\sum_x p_{X,Y}(x,y)",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "d170ca8a-04a5-51a0-aef4-b96de1b99cf7"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 2 · Row and column totals ★ (Lecture 17)",
   "prompt": "Find $p_X$ and $p_Y$.\n\n| | $y=0$ | $y=1$ | $y=2$ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $x=0$ | $0.10$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n| $x=1$ | $0.20$ | $0.30$ | $0.20$ |",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Row totals** give $p_X$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}p_X(0)=0.10+0.15+0.05=0.30 \\\\ p_X(1)=0.20+0.30+0.20=0.70\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Column totals** give $p_Y$.",
     "latex": "p_Y(0)=0.30,\\quad p_Y(1)=0.45,\\quad p_Y(2)=0.25"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Check:** each marginal adds to $1$. Both are $0$ at any other value.",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$p_X=0.30,\\ 0.70$; $p_Y=0.30,\\ 0.45,\\ 0.25$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "951581da-5f56-4a86-9c61-b84ad87d4f7f",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "9288de14-f4e8-4c3c-8f12-d6e7473e62a7"
    }
   ],
   "id": "323301c3-d5a8-5b60-ac99-391ff73a9344"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "tone": "warning",
   "text": "Read the labels. If $y$ is down the side, the **row** totals are $p_Y$.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "89044b27-e404-55fb-97c5-35aed8a0c4b0"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 2 · Marginals, then use them",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "Find $p_X$, $p_Y$, $P(X\\ge2)$.\n\n| | $x=1$ | $x=2$ | $x=3$ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $y=0$ | $0.10$ | $0.20$ | $0.10$ |\n| $y=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.20$ |",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "Here $x$ is across the top, so **column totals** give $p_X$.",
     "latex": "p_X(1)=0.25,\\quad p_X(2)=0.45,\\quad p_X(3)=0.30"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Row totals** give $p_Y$.",
     "latex": "p_Y(0)=0.40,\\quad p_Y(1)=0.60"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Add** the marginal for $x=2,3$.",
     "latex": "P(X\\ge2)=0.45+0.30=0.75"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$p_X=0.25,\\,0.45,\\,0.30$; $p_Y=0.40,\\,0.60$; $0.75$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "834d2a5b-e0a7-5e8e-af8a-e942c81f73e2"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "A3 · Checking independence",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "62be8335-49be-5e7e-b6fb-9b9ee8c28762"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Independent means every cell = its row total × its column total.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "9e85760b-55af-4ca4-9d59-71e1035a301f",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "1e46f773-4923-484d-84b8-364e440a75f3"
    }
   ],
   "id": "500a1e36-1f4a-5845-b257-d4f03344ff10"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "p_{X,Y}(x,y)=p_X(x)\\,p_Y(y)\\quad\\text{for EVERY }(x,y)",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "e3788dd5-ba24-5fac-b40e-5c8942c6c3b4"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "**Dependent:** show one cell that fails. Done.",
    "**Independent:** you must check every cell.",
    "**Shortcut:** a $0$ cell whose row and column totals are not $0$ means dependent."
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "e6c8d319-c89a-5589-a558-54f67a0eb5bb"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 3 · Every cell passes ★ (Lecture 19)",
   "prompt": "Are $X$ and $Y$ independent?\n\n| | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n|---|---|---|\n| $X=0$ | $0.12$ | $0.18$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.28$ | $0.42$ |",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Marginals.**",
     "latex": "p_X=0.30,\\ 0.70\\qquad p_Y=0.40,\\ 0.60"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Check all 4 cells.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}0.30\\times0.40=0.12\\ \\checkmark\\qquad0.30\\times0.60=0.18\\ \\checkmark \\\\ 0.70\\times0.40=0.28\\ \\checkmark\\qquad0.70\\times0.60=0.42\\ \\checkmark\\end{gathered}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "Independent",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "9e85760b-55af-4ca4-9d59-71e1035a301f",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "1e46f773-4923-484d-84b8-364e440a75f3"
    }
   ],
   "id": "ff7e53c7-efdf-5b40-afd3-3e7335569270"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The Lecture 17 table (A2) is **dependent**: $p_X(0)\\,p_Y(0)=0.30\\times0.30=0.09\\ne0.10$.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "ed1f949d-d3b4-50fb-ad21-296b08fe39f4"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 3 · Independent or not?",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "**(a)** \n\n| | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n|---|---|---|\n| $X=0$ | $0.06$ | $0.14$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.24$ | $0.56$ |\n\n**(b)** The coin table from the A1 Try it.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Marginals** $p_X=0.20,\\,0.80$ and $p_Y=0.30,\\,0.70$. **Check all 4.**",
     "latex": "0.06,\\ 0.14,\\ 0.24,\\ 0.56\\ \\text{all match}\\ \\checkmark"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Zero cell:** $p_{X,Y}(2,0)=0$, but $p_X(2)\\,p_Y(0)=\\tfrac14\\cdot\\tfrac12=\\tfrac18\\ne0$.",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** independent\n\n**(b)** dependent",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "9a40a7a9-d868-5ab7-b665-c554c67c5816"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Part B · Continuous (PDFs)",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "b7b25c27-3f68-50db-9a44-3d46c487029f"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Same ideas as Part A. Add up cells → **integrate**.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "f5533cb2-1e96-5373-8af5-60d0dd37dff2"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "B1 · Joint PDFs and finding $c$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "67f20c4c-a705-5748-9c10-de1d21830616"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The joint PDF $f_{X,Y}(x,y)$ is a height over the $xy$-plane. Probability = volume under it. Total volume $=1$, which gives $c$.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "0f47f931-b362-40d3-8be9-68ad8c24477a",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "d92b2d3b-f156-4f34-a100-526b519600ee"
    }
   ],
   "id": "d2f8ea83-7252-5116-9009-d11405b05e50"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "\\iint_{\\text{region}} f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy=1",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "b86be0bf-bd3c-50da-953e-18fb65b6df43"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Shortcut.** On a rectangle, if $f$ is an $x$-part times a $y$-part, integrate each part alone and multiply.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "8c93b555-ec74-5433-85e9-e94a735e5180"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 4 · Find $c$ ★ (Tutorial 8 Q1)",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=c\\,xy$ for $0\\le x\\le1,\\ 0\\le y\\le2$, and $0$ otherwise. Find $c$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Rectangle** and $xy$ splits. Integrate each part.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}\\int_0^1x\\,dx=\\frac12 \\\\ \\int_0^2y\\,dy=2\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Set the volume to $1$.**",
     "latex": "c\\cdot\\frac12\\cdot2=1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad c=1"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$c=1$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "7d80bdef-0a85-4aa8-8247-f4431ad8aec6",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "07a91314-e9cd-45cd-b397-35b10dd7bfd3"
    }
   ],
   "id": "0940f9ab-c906-54e4-aa38-16e769c90b5d"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 4 · Two more $c$’s",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "**(a)** $f=k(x+y)$ on $0\\le x\\le1,\\ 0\\le y\\le1$ (Tutorial 8 Q8).\n\n**(b)** $f=c$ (a constant) on the triangle $0\\le y\\le x\\le2$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) $x+y$ does not split, so integrate in two steps.",
     "latex": "k\\int_0^1\\Big(x+\\frac12\\Big)dx=k\\Big(\\frac12+\\frac12\\Big)=k=1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) A flat $f$: volume $=c\\times$ area. The triangle has area $\\tfrac12\\cdot2\\cdot2=2$.",
     "latex": "2c=1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad c=\\frac12"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $k=1$\n\n**(b)** $c=\\tfrac12$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "7d80bdef-0a85-4aa8-8247-f4431ad8aec6",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "3ab01077-9980-4b23-ba3e-e7135c520c63"
    }
   ],
   "id": "295c2b82-e921-58bd-a286-7d34e43368c2"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "B2 · Double integrals and bounds",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "f00908a8-1f45-5ae4-a782-c642b781d54a"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "P\\big((X,Y)\\in A\\big)=\\iint_A f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "0f47f931-b362-40d3-8be9-68ad8c24477a",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "d92b2d3b-f156-4f34-a100-526b519600ee"
    }
   ],
   "id": "7995f781-c167-599a-b28c-81d6a1c952c9"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The limits are the hard part. Do this every time:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "819c145b-08b3-5829-9338-ca5a109942ce"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "**Sketch** where $f\\ne0$, plus the event’s edge (e.g. the line $x+y=1$).",
    "**Slice:** a vertical line at $x$. Where it enters and leaves the shaded part = the $dy$ limits.",
    "**Sweep:** first to last $x$ that has a slice = the $dx$ limits.",
    "**Integrate** $dy$ first (treat $x$ as a number), then $dx$."
   ],
   "ordered": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "456726a8-13d1-5ecb-959e-51e6a9365148"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Drag the slice. Where does it start and stop?",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "6a0227d8-44e1-56ab-8e31-b6ccf7391778"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "```graph\ntitle \"The event $X+Y<1$ inside the unit square\"\nx -0.2 1.3 label=\"$x$\"\ny -0.2 1.3 label=\"$y$\"\nequal\nregion \"(x>0)*(x<1)*(y>0)*(y<1)\" color=1 label=\"the square where $f\\ne0$\"\nregion \"(x>0)*(y>0)*(x+y<1)\" color=2 label=\"the event $X+Y<1$\"\nslider s 0 1 0.3 label=\"$x$\"\nsegment \"s\" \"0\" \"s\" \"1-s\" color=3 label=\"slice: $y$ from $0$ to $1-x$\"\n```",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "5d86d104-2a45-52fc-9bb1-e31f30488e43"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 5 · Probability under a slanted line ★ (Tutorial 7 Q5)",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=x+y$ for $0<x<1,\\ 0<y<1$. Find $P(X+Y<1)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Sketch:** the triangle under the line $y=1-x$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Slice** at $x$: $y$ from $0$ to $1-x$. **Sweep:** $x$ from $0$ to $1$.",
     "latex": "P=\\int_0^1\\!\\!\\int_0^{1-x}(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Inner** ($dy$).",
     "latex": "\\int_0^{1-x}(x+y)\\,dy=x(1-x)+\\frac{(1-x)^2}{2}=\\frac{1-x^2}{2}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Outer** ($dx$).",
     "latex": "\\int_0^1\\frac{1-x^2}{2}\\,dx=\\frac12\\Big(1-\\frac13\\Big)=\\frac13"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\tfrac13$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "79f52518-90e0-41df-b0b0-5800904bbe9b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "0fbffb43-2956-498c-9f5d-b1a897b31fdd"
    }
   ],
   "id": "06ff6b5c-d1fd-59d8-b959-121156fff00b"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 5 · Two regions ★ (Tutorial 8 Q1, Q8)",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "**(a)** $f=xy$ on $0\\le x\\le1,\\ 0\\le y\\le2$. Find $P(X^2+Y^2\\le1)$.\n\n**(b)** $f=x+y$ on the unit square. Find $P(Y<X^2)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Sketch:** a quarter circle of radius $1$. **Slice:** $y$ from $0$ to $\\sqrt{1-x^2}$, for $0\\le x\\le1$.",
     "latex": "\\int_0^1\\!\\!\\int_0^{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}xy\\,dy\\,dx=\\int_0^1\\frac{x(1-x^2)}{2}\\,dx=\\frac18"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Slice:** $y$ from $0$ to $x^2$, for $0\\le x\\le1$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}\\int_0^1\\!\\!\\int_0^{x^2}(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx=\\int_0^1\\Big(x^3+\\frac{x^4}{2}\\Big)dx \\\\ =\\frac14+\\frac1{10}=\\frac7{20}\\end{gathered}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $\\tfrac18$\n\n**(b)** $\\tfrac7{20}$",
   "citations": [
    {
