   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "For the next example: drag both slices. Which ends move?\n\n```graph\ntitle \"Slices through $-1\\le x\\le1,\\ x^2\\le y\\le1$\"\nx -1.3 1.3 label=\"$x$\"\ny -0.2 1.3 label=\"$y$\"\nequal\nregion \"(y>x^2)*(y<1)\" color=1 label=\"where $f_{X,Y}\\ne0$\"\nslider s -1 1 0.5 label=\"$x$\"\nslider t 0 1 0.5 label=\"$y$\"\nsegment \"s\" \"s^2\" \"s\" \"1\" color=2 label=\"vertical: $y$ from $x^2$ to $1$\"\nsegment \"-sqrt(t)\" \"t\" \"sqrt(t)\" \"t\" color=3 label=\"horizontal: $x$ from $-\\sqrt y$ to $\\sqrt y$\"\n```",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "d62a268d-c223-510d-a757-78907aaa559b"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 6 · Curved region ★ (Lecture 18)",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=\\dfrac{5y}{4}$ for $-1\\le x\\le1,\\ x^2\\le y\\le1$, and $0$ otherwise. Find $f_X$ and $f_Y$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**$f_X$:** vertical slice, $y$ from $x^2$ to $1$.",
     "latex": "f_X(x)=\\int_{x^2}^{1}\\frac{5y}{4}\\,dy=\\frac58\\big(1-x^4\\big),\\qquad -1\\le x\\le1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**$f_Y$:** horizontal slice. $x^2\\le y$ means $-\\sqrt y\\le x\\le\\sqrt y$.",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=\\int_{-\\sqrt y}^{\\sqrt y}\\frac{5y}{4}\\,dx=\\frac{5y}{4}\\cdot2\\sqrt y=\\frac52y^{3/2},\\qquad 0\\le y\\le1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Range:** both are $0$ outside those intervals.",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$f_X=\\tfrac58(1-x^4)$ on $[-1,1]$; $f_Y=\\tfrac52y^{3/2}$ on $[0,1]$",
