  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 1 · [10 marks] A table with $c$",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "| | $y=0$ | $y=1$ | $y=2$ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $x=1$ | $0.10$ | $0.20$ | $c$ |\n| $x=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.30$ | $0.15$ |\n\n**(a)** Find $c$. (2 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $p_X(x)$ and $p_Y(y)$. (3 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $P(X+Y\\le2)$ and $F_{X,Y}(1,1)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(d)** Are $X$ and $Y$ independent? Justify. (3 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Cells add to $1$.**",
     "latex": "0.90+c=1\\ \\Rightarrow\\ c=0.10"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Row / column totals.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}p_X(1)=0.40,\\quad p_X(2)=0.60 \\\\ p_Y(0)=0.25,\\quad p_Y(1)=0.50,\\quad p_Y(2)=0.25\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) $x+y\\le2$: cells $(1,0),(1,1),(2,0)$. $F(1,1)$: $x\\le1,\\ y\\le1$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}P(X+Y\\le2)=0.10+0.20+0.15=0.45 \\\\ F_{X,Y}(1,1)=0.10+0.20=0.30\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **Check all 6 cells.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}0.4(0.25)=0.10,\\ \\ 0.4(0.5)=0.20,\\ \\ 0.4(0.25)=0.10 \\\\ 0.6(0.25)=0.15,\\ \\ 0.6(0.5)=0.30,\\ \\ 0.6(0.25)=0.15\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "All match → **independent**.",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $0.10$\n\n**(b)** $0.4,\\,0.6$; $0.25,\\,0.5,\\,0.25$\n\n**(c)** $0.45$; $0.30$\n\n**(d)** independent",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "dd45465d-3b38-5328-9f52-07fb63bf22d3"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 2 · [10 marks] Build the table from coins",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "A fair coin is tossed 3 times. $X$ = number of heads in tosses 1–2, $Y$ = number of heads in tosses 2–3.\n\n**(a)** List the outcomes and write the joint PMF table. (4 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $p_X$ and $p_Y$. (2 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $P(X=Y)$. (1 mark)\n\n**(d)** Are $X$ and $Y$ independent? Justify. (3 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **8 outcomes**, each $\\tfrac18$. As $(x,y)$: $HHH(2,2)$, $HHT(2,1)$, $HTH(1,1)$, $HTT(1,0)$, $THH(1,2)$, $THT(1,1)$, $TTH(0,1)$, $TTT(0,0)$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Count** each pair (in eighths). Rows $x=0,1,2$; columns $y=0,1,2$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}x=0:\\ \\ 1,\\ 1,\\ 0 \\\\ x=1:\\ \\ 1,\\ 2,\\ 1 \\\\ x=2:\\ \\ 0,\\ 1,\\ 1\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Totals.**",
     "latex": "p_X=p_Y=\\frac28,\\ \\frac48,\\ \\frac28\\quad(\\text{at }0,1,2)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Diagonal.**",
     "latex": "P(X=Y)=\\frac{1+2+1}{8}=\\frac12"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **Zero cell** $(0,2)$:",
     "latex": "p_{X,Y}(0,2)=0\\ne\\frac28\\cdot\\frac28=p_X(0)\\,p_Y(2)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "→ **dependent** (they share toss 2).",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(b)** $\\tfrac14,\\tfrac12,\\tfrac14$ each\n\n**(c)** $\\tfrac12$\n\n**(d)** dependent",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "748cfd4e-22ef-503c-b096-0d8183babf3e"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 3 · [10 marks] A triangle ★ (Tutorial 7 Q6)",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=24xy$ for $x\\ge0,\\ y\\ge0,\\ x+y\\le1$, and $0$ otherwise.\n\n**(a)** Sketch the region. (1 mark)\n\n**(b)** Show it is a valid joint PDF. (3 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $f_X(x)$. (3 marks)\n\n**(d)** Are $X$ and $Y$ independent? Explain. (3 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Sketch:** the triangle with corners $(0,0)$, $(1,0)$, $(0,1)$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) $24xy\\ge0$ there. **Volume:** slice $y$ from $0$ to $1-x$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}\\int_0^1\\!\\!\\int_0^{1-x}24xy\\,dy\\,dx=\\int_0^1 12x(1-x)^2\\,dx \\\\ =12\\Big(\\frac12-\\frac23+\\frac14\\Big)=1\\ \\checkmark\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **The inner integral above** is $f_X$.",
     "latex": "f_X(x)=12x(1-x)^2,\\quad 0\\le x\\le1;\\quad 0\\text{ otherwise}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **Not a rectangle → dependent.** At $(0.9,0.9)$, $f_{X,Y}=0$ but $f_X(0.9)\\,f_Y(0.9)>0$ (by symmetry $f_Y=12y(1-y)^2$).",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(c)** $12x(1-x)^2$ on $[0,1]$\n\n**(d)** dependent",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "79f52518-90e0-41df-b0b0-5800904bbe9b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "0fbffb43-2956-498c-9f5d-b1a897b31fdd"
    }
   ],
   "id": "25d7d34c-4771-5080-a500-782f01e633e4"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 4 · [10 marks] Find $k$, marginals, CDF ★ (Tutorial 8 Q8)",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=k(x+y)$ for $0\\le x\\le1,\\ 0\\le y\\le1$, and $0$ otherwise.\n\n**(a)** Find $k$. (2 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $f_X$ and $f_Y$. (2 marks)\n\n**(c)** Are $X$ and $Y$ independent? (2 marks)\n\n**(d)** Find $F_{X,Y}(x,y)$ for $0\\le x,y\\le1$ and $F_X(x)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(e)** Find $P(X<Y)$. (2 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Volume $=1$.**",
     "latex": "k\\int_0^1\\!\\!\\int_0^1(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx=k=1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Integrate the other variable away.**",
     "latex": "f_X(x)=x+\\frac12,\\quad f_Y(y)=y+\\frac12\\quad(\\text{on }[0,1])"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Doesn’t split.** At $(0,0)$: $f_Xf_Y=\\tfrac14\\ne0$ → dependent.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **From $(0,0)$**, then the top edge $y=1$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}F_{X,Y}=\\frac{x^2y+xy^2}{2} \\\\ F_X(x)=\\frac{x^2+x}{2}\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(e) **Slice** at $x$: $y$ from $x$ to $1$.",
     "latex": "\\int_0^1\\!\\!\\int_x^1(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx=\\int_0^1\\Big(x+\\frac12-\\frac{3x^2}{2}\\Big)dx=\\frac12+\\frac12-\\frac12=\\frac12"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $1$\n\n**(b)** $x+\\tfrac12$, $y+\\tfrac12$\n\n**(c)** dependent\n\n**(d)** $\\tfrac{x^2y+xy^2}2$; $\\tfrac{x^2+x}2$\n\n**(e)** $\\tfrac12$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "7d80bdef-0a85-4aa8-8247-f4431ad8aec6",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "3ab01077-9980-4b23-ba3e-e7135c520c63"
    }
   ],
   "id": "29ed2257-ff7d-5259-bc49-451298ef2010"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 5 · [10 marks] Exponential pair",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=c\\,e^{-x-2y}$ for $x>0,\\ y>0$, and $0$ otherwise.\n\n**(a)** Find $c$. (2 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $f_X$ and $f_Y$. (3 marks)\n\n**(c)** Are $X$ and $Y$ independent? (1 mark)\n\n**(d)** Find $F_{X,Y}(x,y)$ and $F_X(x)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(e)** Find $P(X<Y)$. (2 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Splits** ($e^{-x}\\cdot e^{-2y}$) on a (infinite) rectangle.",
     "latex": "c\\int_0^\\infty e^{-x}dx\\int_0^\\infty e^{-2y}dy=c\\cdot1\\cdot\\frac12=1\\ \\Rightarrow\\ c=2"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Integrate away.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}f_X(x)=\\int_0^\\infty2e^{-x-2y}dy=e^{-x}\\quad(x>0) \\\\ f_Y(y)=\\int_0^\\infty2e^{-x-2y}dx=2e^{-2y}\\quad(y>0)\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) $f_Xf_Y=2e^{-x-2y}=f_{X,Y}$ → **independent**.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **From $(0,0)$.** Then $y\\to\\infty$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}F_{X,Y}=\\int_0^x e^{-u}du\\int_0^y2e^{-2v}dv=(1-e^{-x})(1-e^{-2y}) \\\\ F_X(x)=1-e^{-x},\\quad x>0\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(e) **Slice:** $y$ from $x$ to $\\infty$.",
     "latex": "\\int_0^\\infty e^{-x}\\Big(\\int_x^\\infty2e^{-2y}dy\\Big)dx=\\int_0^\\infty e^{-3x}\\,dx=\\frac13"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $2$\n\n**(b)** $e^{-x}$, $2e^{-2y}$\n\n**(c)** independent\n\n**(d)** $(1-e^{-x})(1-e^{-2y})$; $1-e^{-x}$\n\n**(e)** $\\tfrac13$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "e587745f-91fd-51c8-815d-2f2fdde24a83"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 6 · [10 marks] A flat triangle",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=c$ for $0\\le y\\le x\\le2$, and $0$ otherwise.\n\n**(a)** Find $c$. (2 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y(y)$. (4 marks)\n\n**(c)** Are $X$ and $Y$ independent? (2 marks)\n\n**(d)** Find $P(X+Y\\le2)$. (2 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Area** of the triangle is $\\tfrac12\\cdot2\\cdot2=2$.",
     "latex": "2c=1\\ \\Rightarrow\\ c=\\frac12"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **$f_X$:** $y$ from $0$ to $x$. **$f_Y$:** $x$ from $y$ to $2$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}f_X(x)=\\int_0^x\\frac12\\,dy=\\frac x2,\\qquad0\\le x\\le2 \\\\ f_Y(y)=\\int_y^2\\frac12\\,dx=\\frac{2-y}{2},\\qquad0\\le y\\le2\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Triangle → dependent.** At $(0.5,\\,1.5)$: $f_{X,Y}=0$ (needs $y\\le x$), but $f_X(0.5)f_Y(1.5)=\\tfrac14\\cdot\\tfrac14>0$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **Sketch:** inside the triangle and under $x+y=2$. Slice horizontally: $x$ from $y$ to $2-y$, for $0\\le y\\le1$.",
     "latex": "\\int_0^1\\!\\!\\int_y^{2-y}\\frac12\\,dx\\,dy=\\int_0^1(1-y)\\,dy=\\frac12"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $\\tfrac12$\n\n**(b)** $\\tfrac x2$; $\\tfrac{2-y}2$\n\n**(c)** dependent\n\n**(d)** $\\tfrac12$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "f8cfe856-c5bd-5742-bb0d-c8870536cb33"
  },
